{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '150,240p' collab/exception-track/1794446270000-architect-php-r1r2r3-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md; cat test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj; sed -n '1,260p' test/yang/call/php_exception_test.clj; sed -n '1,130p' test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj; sed -n '337,405p' test/yang/call/conformance.clj; sed -n '355,430p' test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '150,240p' collab/exception-track/1794446270000-architect-php-r1r2r3-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md; cat test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj; sed -n '1,260p' test/yang/call/php_exception_test.clj; sed -n '1,130p' test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj; sed -n '337,405p' test/yang/call/conformance.clj; sed -n '355,430p' test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\"","aggregated_output":"The cell mechanism matches the accepted Python adoption:\n\n- Atomic reserved-door allocation at prelude.cljc:4618 places provenance on the actual\n  identity cell under `:php/obj`; no intermediate holder is used.\n- Memberless/missing classes refuse at :4611 instead of producing an unmarkable retained\n  map. The ordinary non-retained `php/make-error` fallback remains a different path.\n- Reader at :4642 passes the identity cell to `cell/dsg__provenance`, with no attribute,\n  ordinal, content equality, or wrapper-supplied condition consulted.\n- Both doors are declared at :99. Firsthand export inspection found zero `php.rt`\n  exports. The r2 lexical retention-store definition, installer, placeholders and init\n  hook are absent from the final prelude.\n- VM allocation stores value/seal/provenance together\n  (src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2811); authenticated read is total (:2828).\n  `heap-write` changes the value while preserving provenance (:2444).\n  GC traces the provenance sibling (:2628).\n\nConsequently contents-cloning into a fresh unmarked cell carries no provenance;\nmutation of the genuine cell's visible contents does not replace the association.\nThe PHP pins at php_exception_test.clj:235 and :268 exercise these respective attacks.\nThere is no source-readable companion condition to overwrite or extracted companion seal\nto stamp onto another cell. The old store's lookup/growth residual is removed; ordinary\nheap reachability retains the condition.\n\nThis closes the mechanism defects exposed by the JS ce99e65e/31287b17 fix arc, including\ncompanion mutation and metadata-based authority. JS's eventual private identity membership\nand hidden helper exports are the relevant comparison (current JS prelude :4131, :4141).\nBut PHP's exported receiver leaves the transitive minting-authority hole open. Thus the\nadoption as a whole is not equivalent to the accepted Python/JS closure of that edge.\n\nNil provenance is refused by the VM (:2812). The absent PHP pre-guard remains the same\ndocumented low-priority behavior split accepted for Python (8018005d merge record);\nit is not an additional blocker here.\n\n## Item 4 — Disclosed r2 lane findings: disposition\n\n### Shutdown/global release: prefer an instrument-shape repair\n\nThe diagnosis is supported by unchanged implementation: `php/run-main` runs shutdown at\nprelude.cljc:5758; shutdown calls release-globals (:4376), which explicitly unsets every\nglobal (:4338). The kit source initializes `$original` at module scope\n(test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:60) and exports functions reading it (:61).\n\nPreference on record: keep PHP lifecycle behavior and change the kit-owned setup so the\nidentity-bearing payload is created after unit shutdown, before the observations, as the\ndirected source's `seed` already does (php_exception_test.clj:109). Retain the original\npayload-identity/once/after assertions and use one real object across all relevant\nobservations. Do not weaken expectations or silently mark these rows green. The steward\nowns that fixture change and ledger disposition; this review does not implement it.\n\nThe disclosed 18 assertion failures are structurally plausible: six fresh-egress failures,\nthree local-reception failures, and nine duplicated batch failures. I did not independently\nrerun or compare their failure bytes against the old base.\n\n### Concurrent-content stall: no direct core change, possible workload interaction\n\nNo dao.jing, query, linker, scheduler, content store, or shared kit implementation changes\nin the reviewed diff. The kit explicitly runs three futures reading shared published content\n(test/yang/call/conformance.clj:468). Its cross-frontend reproduction does not by itself\nexclude PHP interaction, since PHP publication is shared by those legs.\n\nThe larger PHP module, per-entry result-cell allocation (:2712), bridge/capture work,\nand provenance allocation can alter content sizes, allocation pressure and scheduling.\nThose are plausible triggers for an existing stall, not proof of a PHP concurrency bug.\nThe disclosed base-fast/head-hang sample should stay on record. No evidence here warrants\nmoving a dao.jing repair into this PHP round. Keep the shiva clean-content acceptance run\nand bounded per-leg diagnosis; do not treat a retry as proof the stall is fixed.\n\n## Item 5 — Scope and gate plausibility: ACCEPT WITH RECORD CORRECTIONS/LIMITS\n\nThe actual diff is 10 files: the PHP prelude, the new PHP boundary-test namespace, and\neight exception-track briefs/spec/findings records. Runtime regions are function entry,\nClosure entry, reception through the three helpers, retention helpers, host-door declaration,\nand the seeded exception hierarchy. This is consistent with the supplied PHP round and\nadoption briefs. No shared kit, design doctrine, scanner golden, ledger, or other frontend\nimplementation was edited. `git diff --check 0e666a3f..4939a3ae` passed.\n\nThe referenced region registry\n`collab/exception-track/1794343000000-exception-track-surface-registry.md` is absent from\nthis worktree and from the reviewed base. Its literal region list cannot be certified here;\nscope was checked against the available binding briefs and actual diff instead.\n\nGate tables are plausible as scoped engineer reports, not independently reproduced gate\nresults. The hard-rule parity pin (:298) uses the kit boundary and parsed PHP bare rethrow,\nasserts the fully qualified reason and condition identity, and checks all three backends.\nThe clone/mutation pins inspect guest identity before rendering. Test data and assertions\nwere not weakened by r2/r3. The reported Node/Dart/remote and slow-corpus gaps are explicit.\n\nCorrection: there are **13 PHP fixtures**, confirmed by loading the actual contract data,\nnot 15. The batch test at php_exception_test.clj:327 has\n`1 + 13 * (1 + 3) = 53` assertions. Three failing fixtures therefore leave **10 green\nfixtures**, not “the other 12” in r2's gate table and r3 findings:83. This arithmetic\n(ns yang.call.exception-contract-test\n  \"Intentionally red until exception rounds 1–4 repair the runtimes. Never\n   invert assertions or encode today's divergences as expected behavior.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing do-report]]\n            [yang.call.exception-contract :as contract]\n            [yang.call.exception-probes :as probes]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as js-prelude]))\n\n\n(defn- check-frontend\n  [frontend]\n  (let [observations (probes/run-frontend frontend)]\n    (doseq [{:keys [id expected] :as fixture}\n            (filter #(= frontend (:frontend %)) contract/fixtures)]\n      (testing (str id \" gates=\" (:gates fixture))\n        (try\n          (let [results (get observations id)]\n            (println \"PROVENANCE\"\n                     (pr-str {:id id :gates (:gates fixture) :frontends (:frontends fixture)\n                              :expected expected\n                              :results (update-vals results #(if (instance? Throwable %)\n                                                               {:host/error (.getMessage ^Throwable %)\n                                                                :host/data (ex-data %)} %))\n                              :status (update-vals results #(cond (instance? Throwable %) :error\n                                                                  (= expected %) :green :else :red))}))\n            (doseq [[backend actual] results]\n              (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n                (do-report {:type :error :message (str id \" \" backend \" operational failure\")\n                            :expected expected :actual actual})\n                (is (= expected actual) (str id \" \" backend)))))\n          (catch Exception e\n            (do-report {:type :error :message (str id \" boundary fixture failed to execute\")\n                        :expected expected :actual e})))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r1 ::contract/r2 ::contract/r3 ::contract/r5}\n           :frontends #{:python}}\n  python-provenance-test\n  (check-frontend :python))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r1 ::contract/r2 ::contract/r3 ::contract/r5}\n           :frontends #{:php}}\n  php-provenance-test\n  (check-frontend :php))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r1 ::contract/r3 ::contract/r5}\n           :frontends #{:typescript}}\n  typescript-provenance-test\n  (check-frontend :typescript))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r1 ::contract/r3 ::contract/r5}\n           :frontends #{:clojure}}\n  clojure-provenance-test\n  (check-frontend :clojure))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n  typescript-minted-forgery-test\n  ;; A source-minted error-looking cell (and a companion-layout mimic with\n  ;; an attacker-chosen seal) thrown through the donor's raise_value must\n  ;; NOT forward its forged condition: the bridge delivers a fresh\n  ;; :yang.call/thrown carrying the minted cell itself.\n  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-forgery :minted)]\n    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"minted forgery \" backend \" operational failure\")\n                  :expected {:minted-refused true :mimic-refused true} :actual actual})\n      (is (= {:minted-refused true :mimic-refused true} actual)\n          (str \"minted forgery \" backend)))))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n  typescript-mutation-substitution-test\n  ;; The architect's round-2 attack: a genuine wrapper obtained via\n  ;; `retain`, its wrapper-reachable provenance overwritten with a\n  ;; forged condition, rethrown from a new activation. The ORIGINAL\n  ;; condition must still forward; the forged one must not cross.\n  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-identity-store :mutated)]\n    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"mutation substitution \" backend \" operational failure\")\n                  :expected {:retained true :original-forwarded true} :actual actual})\n      (is (= {:retained true :original-forwarded true} actual)\n          (str \"mutation substitution \" backend)))))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n  typescript-extracted-seal-stamping-test\n  ;; A new wrapper stamped with whatever seal a genuine wrapper's\n  ;; references expose, with a companion back-referencing itself, must\n  ;; end as ordinary :yang.call/thrown carrying the minted cell, never\n  ;; as a retained forwarding.\n  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-identity-store :extracted-seal)]\n    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"extracted-seal stamping \" backend \" operational failure\")\n                  :expected {:retained true :stamped-refused true} :actual actual})\n      (is (= {:retained true :stamped-refused true} actual)\n          (str \"extracted-seal stamping \" backend)))))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n  typescript-store-root-unreachability-test\n  ;; Guest side: a genuine wrapper carries no provenance, condition or\n  ;; seal slot, and no global name holds the store or a seal.\n  ;; Host side: the private store is not a runtime key and neither\n  ;; installed retention name is a module export, so admitted source\n  ;; cannot reach it by enumerating either, and no frozen pre-init\n  ;; export binding can silently answer for it.\n  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-identity-store :store-root)]\n    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"store-root unreachability \" backend \" operational failure\")\n                  :expected {:retained true :wrapper-clean true :globals-clean true} :actual actual})\n      (is (= {:retained true :wrapper-clean true :globals-clean true} actual)\n          (str \"store-root unreachability \" backend))))\n  (is (not-any? #(str/includes? (str %) \"retained\") js-prelude/runtime-keys)\n      \"no retained store/seal runtime key for admitted source to name\")\n  (is (not (contains? js-prelude/module-exports 'retained-condition))\n      \"retained-condition is not a module export: no frozen pre-init binding\")\n  (is (not (contains? js-prelude/module-exports 'raise-protocol))\n      \"raise-protocol is not a module export: no frozen pre-init binding\"))\n\n\n(deftest ^{:slow true :gates #{::contract/r5} :frontends #{:typescript}}\n  typescript-copied-wrapper-forgery-test\n  ;; A fresh cell carrying a copy of a genuine protocol wrapper's complete\n  ;; contents, thrown from another activation, must NOT forward the\n  ;; original condition: provenance is bound to the genuine wrapper's\n  ;; identity, not to its copyable contents.\n  (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-typescript-forgery :copied)]\n    (if (instance? Throwable actual)\n      (do-report {:type :error :message (str \"copied wrapper \" backend \" operational failure\")\n                  :expected {:retained true :copy-refused true} :actual actual})\n      (is (= {:retained true :copy-refused true} actual)\n          (str \"copied wrapper \" backend)))))\n(ns yang.call.php-exception-test\n  \"PHP boundary pins for ruling v2 R1+R2+R3 (one coherent round). Receivers\n   and rethrows are parsed source; malformed protocol delivery uses the\n   shared boundary kit. The focused local gate for the exception-php-r1r2r3\n   round: the php subset of the shiva acceptance instrument, never a\n   substitute for the full ledger.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yang.call.conformance :as kit]\n            [yang.call.exception-contract :as contract]\n            [yang.call.exception-legs :as legs]\n            [yang.call.exception-probes :as probes]\n            [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]))\n\n\n(defn- check-fixture\n  \"Run one php fixture isolated on all three vector VMs and assert its\n   compliant `:expected` value on each backend.\"\n  [id]\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) contract/fixtures))]\n    (testing (str id)\n      (doseq [[backend actual] (probes/run-fixture fixture)]\n        (is (= (:expected fixture) actual) (str backend))))))\n\n\n(defn- check-leg\n  \"Run one directed source pair/scenario and assert `legs/expected` per VM.\"\n  [id]\n  (let [leg (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) contract/pair-matrix))]\n    (testing (str id)\n      (doseq [[backend actual] (legs/run-leg leg)]\n        (is (= (legs/expected leg) actual) (str id \" \" backend))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow php-fresh-egress-test\n  ;; R1: the function entry and the Closure entry read the supplied\n  ;; :yang.call/raise and deliver every escaping exception (and binding\n  ;; failure) exactly once as the thrown condition; nothing runs after.\n  (check-fixture :php/fresh-named)\n  (check-fixture :php/fresh-closure)\n  (check-fixture :php/binding))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow php-foreign-reception-test\n  ;; R2: an already-local Throwable is delivered unchanged (identity kept);\n  ;; an otherwise-foreign payload becomes the generated local\n  ;; ForeignException retaining the complete condition.\n  (check-fixture :php/local-reception)\n  (check-fixture :php/foreign-reception)\n  (check-fixture :php/retained-foreign-lifetime)\n  ;; Directed legs with php as the RECEIVER: typed catch matches the local\n  ;; hierarchy, unchanged rethrow forwards, stored wrappers rethrow from a\n  ;; new activation.\n  (check-leg [:python :php :typed-catch])\n  (check-leg [:python :php :unchanged-rethrow])\n  (check-leg [:python :php :retained-lifetime])\n  (check-leg [:clojure :php :catch-all])\n  ;; The bridge as DONOR: a php escape crossing into a landed frontend.\n  (check-leg [:php :typescript :catch-all]))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow php-protocol-reception-test\n  ;; R3: not-callable / invalid-invocation / unsupported-binding retain the\n  ;; complete condition instead of a fresh Error with selected text; the\n  ;; saved-wrapper rethrow forwards the original condition, no wrapper\n  ;; stacking.\n  (check-fixture :php/protocol-not-callable)\n  (check-fixture :php/protocol-invalid-invocation)\n  (check-fixture :php/protocol-unsupported-binding)\n  (check-fixture :php/saved-protocol-not-callable)\n  (check-fixture :php/saved-protocol-invalid-invocation)\n  (check-fixture :php/saved-protocol-unsupported-binding))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow php-forged-retention-test\n  ;; R5: source-writable attributes never authenticate a retained\n  ;; condition — a forged Exception carrying condition-looking props crosses\n  ;; as a fresh :yang.call/thrown with the forged object as payload.\n  (check-fixture :php/forged-retention))\n\n\n(defn- injected\n  \"The kit's synthetic entry delivering `condition` to the raise exit.\"\n  [condition]\n  (list 'cell/new\n        (list 'assoc {} :yang.call/entry\n              (list 'fn ['invocation]\n                    (list (list 'get 'invocation :yang.call/raise) condition)))))\n\n\n(defn- boundary-call\n  [callee args]\n  (kit/boundary-call-form callee (kit/observation-vector-form args) []))\n\n\n(defn- genuine-wrapper-bindings\n  \"Guest bindings that mint a genuine ForeignException wrapper through php\n   reception: the contract `retain` catches it and returns it normally.\"\n  []\n  ['probe.condition (kit/observation-map-form\n                      {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                       :yang.call/value (list 'cell/new {:foreign/payload :identity})\n                       :yang.call/data {:complete [:extra :evidence]}})\n   'probe.injected (injected 'probe.condition)\n   'probe.retained (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\n   'probe.wrapper (list 'get 'probe.retained :value)])\n\n\n(def ^:private egress-source\n  \"The contract's php exception shapes with the module-level `$original`\n   replaced by a function-seeded global. php's run-main shutdown releases\n   the caller unit's globals when the unit returns (PHP script-end\n   semantics), and the kit's boundary observations run AFTER the caller\n   unit — so a module-level `$original = new Exception(...)` reads back\n   null through `payload()` in this lane (a pre-existing instrument/lane\n   conflict recorded in the round's findings; the base commit behaves the\n   same). A global WRITTEN by a called function after the unit's run\n   persists for the later observation calls, so `seed` mints the\n   identity-bearing original the directed legs below throw, rethrow and\n   retain — the same assertions the three lane-blocked fixtures\n   (:php/fresh-named, :php/fresh-closure, :php/local-reception) make on\n   module-level state. `retain` keeps its wrapper in `$caught`, never\n   touching the original's `$saved`.\"\n  (str \"<?php $saved = null; $caught = null;\"\n       \"function seed() { global $saved; $saved = new Exception('original'); return $saved; }\"\n       \"function payload() { global $saved; return $saved; }\"\n       \"function donor_raise() { global $saved; throw $saved; }\"\n       \"function make_exploder() { return function() { global $saved; throw $saved; }; }\"\n       \"function receive($f) { try { return $f(); } catch (Throwable $e) { throw $e; } }\"\n       \"function retain($f) { global $caught; try { return $f(); }\"\n       \" catch (Throwable $e) { $caught = $e; return $e; } }\"))\n\n\n(defn- run-egress-observation\n  \"The egress source as caller, the python boundary donor beside it, and\n   `observation` appended: all three linked vector VMs.\"\n  [observation]\n  (let [donor (kit/publish-donor! :python contract/boundary-source)]\n    (kit/run-exception-program\n      donor (kit/compose-exception donor [\"boundary_target\"] :php\n                                   egress-source observation))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow php-fresh-egress-directed-test\n  ;; R1, directed (the in-lane form of :php/fresh-named and\n  ;; :php/fresh-closure): the function entry and the Closure entry deliver\n  ;; the escaping source Exception to the supplied raise exit exactly once\n  ;; as {:yang.call/thrown, original} — the payload IS the thrown object.\n  (let [observation\n        (kit/guard-exceptions-form\n          [:php]\n          (list 'let ['probe.seeded (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \"seed\") [])\n                      'original (list 'get 'probe.seeded :value)\n                      'probe.named (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \"donor_raise\") [])\n                      'probe.closure (boundary-call\n                                       (list 'get (boundary-call\n                                                    (kit/export-form :php \"make_exploder\") [])\n                                             :value) [])]\n                (kit/observation-map-form\n                  {:seeded (list '= :return (list 'get 'probe.seeded :route))\n                   :named-transferred (list '= :raise (list 'get 'probe.named :route))\n                   :named-once (list '= 1 (list 'get 'probe.named :transfers))\n                   :named-after (list 'get 'probe.named :after)\n                   :named-reason (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.named :condition)\n                                       :yang.call/reason)\n                   :named-payload-identical\n                   (list '= 'original (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.named :condition)\n                                            :yang.call/value))\n                   :closure-transferred (list '= :raise (list 'get 'probe.closure :route))\n                   :closure-once (list '= 1 (list 'get 'probe.closure :transfers))\n                   :closure-after (list 'get 'probe.closure :after)\n                   :closure-reason (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.closure :condition)\n                                         :yang.call/reason)\n                   :closure-payload-identical\n                   (list '= 'original (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.closure :condition)\n                                            :yang.call/value))})))\n        expected {:seeded true\n                  :named-transferred true :named-once true :named-after false\n                  :named-reason :yang.call/thrown :named-payload-identical true\n                  :closure-transferred true :closure-once true :closure-after false\n                  :closure-reason :yang.call/thrown :closure-payload-identical true}]\n    (doseq [[backend actual] (run-egress-observation observation)]\n      (is (= expected actual) (str backend)))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow php-local-reception-directed-test\n  ;; R2, directed (the in-lane form of :php/local-reception): a thrown\n  ;; condition whose payload is already a php Throwable keeps its ordinary\n  ;; catching and identity — re-raised UNCHANGED (typed catch, unchanged\n  ;; rethrow, returned identity), never wrapped.\n  (let [observation\n        (kit/guard-exceptions-form\n          [:php]\n          (list 'let ['probe.seeded (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \"seed\") [])\n                      'original (list 'get 'probe.seeded :value)\n                      'probe.condition (kit/observation-map-form\n                                         {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                                          :yang.call/value 'original})\n                      'probe.injected (injected 'probe.condition)\n                      'probe.reres (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \"receive\")\n                                                  ['probe.injected])\n                      'probe.rtres (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \"retain\")\n                                                  ['probe.injected])]\n                (kit/observation-map-form\n                  {:seeded (list '= :return (list 'get 'probe.seeded :route))\n                   :rethrow-transferred (list '= :raise (list 'get 'probe.reres :route))\n                   :rethrow-once (list '= 1 (list 'get 'probe.reres :transfers))\n                   :rethrow-reason (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.reres :condition)\n                                         :yang.call/reason)\n                   :rethrow-payload-identical\n                   (list '= 'original (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.reres :condition)\n                                            :yang.call/value))\n                   :retain-returned (list '= :return (list 'get 'probe.rtres :route))\n                   :retain-payload-identical\n                   (list '= 'original (list 'get 'probe.rtres :value))})))\n        expected {:seeded true\n                  :rethrow-transferred true :rethrow-once true\n                  :rethrow-reason :yang.call/thrown\n                  :rethrow-payload-identical true\n                  :retain-returned true :retain-payload-identical true}]\n    (doseq [[backend actual] (run-egress-observation observation)]\n      (is (= expected actual) (str backend)))))\n\n\n(defn- run-provenance-observation\n  \"The contract php source as caller, the python boundary donor beside it,\n   and `observation` appended: all three linked vector VMs.\"\n  [observation]\n  (let [donor (kit/publish-donor! :python contract/boundary-source)]\n    (kit/run-exception-program\n      donor (kit/compose-exception donor [\"boundary_target\"] :php\n                                   (contract/sources :php) observation))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow php-copied-wrapper-forgery-test\n  ;; A fresh state cell carrying a genuine wrapper's complete contents is a\n  ;; DIFFERENT object: provenance is bound to the wrapper's identity (its\n  ;; sealed state-cell reference), never to its copyable contents. Throwing\n  ;; the copy from a new activation must NOT forward the original condition.\n  (let [observation\n        (kit/guard-exceptions-form\n          [:php]\n          (list 'let (into (genuine-wrapper-bindings)\n                           ['probe.copy (list 'assoc {} :php/obj\n                                              (list 'cell/new\n                                                    (list 'cell/get\n                                                          (list 'get 'probe.wrapper :php/obj))))\n                            'probe.result (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \"raise_value\")\n                                                         ['probe.copy])])\n                (kit/observation-map-form\n                  {:retained (list '= :return (list 'get 'probe.retained :route))\n                   :copy-refused\n                   (list 'if (list '= :raise (list 'get 'probe.result :route))\n                         (list 'if (list '= 1 (list 'get 'probe.result :transfers))\n                               (list 'if (list '= :yang.call/thrown\n                                               (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.result :condition)\n                                                     :yang.call/reason))\n                                     (list '= 'probe.copy\n                                           (list 'get (list 'get 'probe.result :condition)\n                                                 :yang.call/value))\n(ns yang.call.exception-contract\n  \"Round 0's executable §8.10.7 provenance contract. Source strings are\n   parsed by the JVM kit, never patched after lowering. Boundary probes\n   alone may manufacture invocations that valid source cannot express.\n   `fixtures` is the acceptance-ledger input; pending is not a passing test.\n   The ruling, rather than today's runtime output, determines `:expected`.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(def frontends #{:clojure :typescript :php :python})\n\n\n(def protocol-reasons\n  [:yang.call/not-callable :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n   :yang.call/unsupported-binding])\n\n\n(def sources\n  \"Every export below is source-produced. `original` is an identity-bearing\n   value, including Clojure's explicit cell. `receive` catches then rethrows unchanged;\n   `retain` returns normally before `later` raises from a new activation.\n   Protocol catch forms are intentionally local catch-all forms. No guessed\n   donor class name participates in reception.\"\n  {:python\n   (str/join \"\\n\"\n             [\"original = ValueError('original')\"\n              \"saved = None\"\n              \"def payload():\" \"    return original\"\n              \"def donor_raise():\" \"    raise original\"\n              \"def make_exploder():\"\n              \"    def inner():\" \"        raise original\" \"    return inner\"\n              \"def needs_argument(x):\" \"    return x\"\n              \"def receive(f):\"\n              \"    try:\" \"        return f()\"\n              \"    except BaseException as e:\" \"        raise\"\n              \"def retain(f):\" \"    global saved\"\n              \"    try:\" \"        f()\"\n              \"    except BaseException as e:\" \"        saved = e\" \"        return e\"\n              \"def later():\" \"    raise saved\"\n              \"def is_foreign(e):\"\n              \"    return isinstance(e, BaseException) and type(e).__name__ == 'ForeignException'\"\n              \"def forged(condition):\"\n              \"    e = Exception('forged')\"\n              \"    e.condition = condition\"\n              \"    e.__yang_call_condition__ = e.condition\"\n              \"    return e\"\n              \"def raise_value(e):\" \"    raise e\" \"\"])\n   :typescript\n   (str \"globalThis.original = {marker: 'original'};\"\n        \"globalThis.saved = null;\"\n        \"globalThis.payload = function() { return original; };\"\n        \"globalThis.donor_raise = function() { throw original; };\"\n        \"globalThis.make_exploder = function() { return () => { throw original; }; };\"\n        \"globalThis.receive = function(f) { try { return f(); } catch (e) { throw e; } };\"\n        \"globalThis.retain = function(f) { try { return f(); } catch (e) { globalThis.saved = e; return e; } };\"\n        \"globalThis.later = function() { throw saved; };\"\n        \"globalThis.raise_value = function(e) { throw e; };\"\n        \"globalThis.echo = function(e) { return e; };\")\n   :php\n   (str \"<?php $original = new Exception('original'); $saved = null;\"\n        \"function payload() { global $original; return $original; }\"\n        \"function donor_raise() { global $original; throw $original; }\"\n        \"function make_exploder() { return function() { global $original; throw $original; }; }\"\n        \"function needs_argument($x) { return $x; }\"\n        \"function receive($f) { try { return $f(); } catch (Throwable $e) { throw $e; } }\"\n        \"function retain($f) { global $saved; try { return $f(); } catch (Throwable $e) { $saved = $e; return $e; } }\"\n        \"function later() { global $saved; throw $saved; }\"\n        \"function is_foreign($e) { return $e instanceof Throwable && get_class($e) === 'ForeignException'; }\"\n        \"function forged($condition) { $e = new Exception('forged'); $e->condition = $condition;\"\n        \" $e->__yang_call_condition__ = $e->condition; return $e; }\"\n        \"function raise_value($e) { throw $e; }\")\n   :clojure\n   (str \"(def original (cell/new :original)) (def saved (cell/new nil)) \"\n        \"(defn payload [] original) (defn donor_raise [] (throw original)) \"\n        \"(defn make_exploder [] (fn [] (throw original))) \"\n        \"(defn needs_argument [x] x) \"\n        \"(defn receive [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e (throw e)))) \"\n        \"(defn retain [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e (cell/set! saved e) e))) \"\n        \"(defn later [] (throw (cell/get saved))) \"\n        \"(defn raise_value [e] (throw e)) (defn echo [e] e)\")})\n\n\n(def boundary-source\n  \"A real Python entry produces unsupported-binding. Other two protocol\n   conditions come from yang.call validation, with malformed positional\n   data supplied only by the boundary probe. This is NOT a source pair.\"\n  \"def boundary_target():\\n    return None\\n\")\n\n\n(defn- fixture\n  [scenario frontend gates expected & [extra]]\n  (merge {:id (keyword (name frontend) (name scenario))\n          :scenario scenario :gates gates :frontends #{frontend}\n          :frontend frontend :source (sources frontend)\n          :expected expected :execution :jvm-linked :round 0}\n         extra))\n\n\n(def fixtures\n  (vec\n    (concat\n      (for [f (sort frontends), kind [:named :closure]]\n        (fixture (keyword (str \"fresh-\" (name kind))) f #{::r1 ::r5}\n                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n                  :reason :yang.call/thrown :payload-identical true}\n                 {:callable-kind kind}))\n      (for [f [:clojure :php :python]]\n        (fixture :binding f #{::r1} {:transferred true :once true :after false\n                                     :reason :yang.call/thrown}))\n      (for [f (sort frontends), reason protocol-reasons]\n        (fixture (keyword (str \"protocol-\" (name reason))) f #{::r3}\n                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\n                 {:protocol-reason reason}))\n      (for [f [:python :php]]\n        (fixture :local-reception f #{::r2}\n                 {:returned true :payload-identical true}))\n      (for [f [:python :php]]\n        (fixture :foreign-reception f #{::r2}\n                 {:returned true :local-foreign-exception true}))\n      (for [f [:python :php]]\n        (fixture :retained-foreign-lifetime f #{::r2 ::r5}\n                 {:retained true :local-foreign-exception true\n                  :transferred true :once true :after false\n                  :condition-identical true :payload-identical true}))\n      (for [f (sort frontends), reason protocol-reasons]\n        (fixture (keyword (str \"saved-protocol-\" (name reason))) f #{::r3 ::r5}\n                 {:retained true :transferred true :once true :after false\n                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\n                 {:protocol-reason reason}))\n(defn compose-exception\n  \"Compose real donor/caller source exactly as `compose` does, optionally\n   followed by an unlowered boundary observation form. The source bodies\n   and their call nodes are untouched. Boundary forms are for provenance\n   assertions and malformed invocations, not substitute source-pair legs.\"\n  ([donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\n   (compose donor exports caller-frontend caller-source))\n  ([donor exports caller-frontend caller-source observation]\n   (u/mark-tails\n     (u/then (compose donor exports caller-frontend caller-source)\n             (u/sexp->uast observation)))))\n\n\n(defn observation-map-form\n  \"Emit a map whose known observation values are guest expressions.\n   sexp->uast intentionally treats a map literal as DATA, including lists\n   and symbols within it. Dynamic boundary observations use explicit assoc,\n   never a transformation of parsed source or a runtime shape detector.\"\n  [entries]\n  (reduce (fn [form [k value]] (list 'assoc form k value)) {} entries))\n\n\n(defn observation-vector-form\n  \"Emit a boundary argument vector of evaluated expressions. Like maps,\n   vectors in sexp->uast are otherwise literal data.\"\n  [expressions]\n  (reduce (fn [form value] (list 'conj form value)) [] expressions))\n\n\n(defn boundary-call-form\n  \"An abortive observer of a public entry, as guest code. All arguments are\n   forms. `options` selects invoke-with when present. A returned envelope\n   is recorded as :return; only the supplied exit records :raise. Transfer\n   count and the after-call sentinel live in task cells. No payload is\n   snapshotted here: assertions must precede rendering.\"\n  ([callee positional named]\n   (boundary-call-form callee positional named nil))\n  ([callee positional named options]\n   (let [phase (gensym \"phase\")\n         transfers (gensym \"transfers\")\n         after (gensym \"after\")\n         escape (gensym \"escape\")\n         condition (gensym \"condition\")\n         returned (gensym \"returned\")\n         raise (list 'fn [condition]\n                     (list 'do\n                           (list 'cell/set! transfers (list '+ 1 (list 'cell/get transfers)))\n                           (list escape\n                                 (observation-map-form\n                                   {:route :raise :condition condition\n                                    :transfers (list 'cell/get transfers)\n                                    :after (list 'cell/get after)}))))\n         invocation (if options\n                      (list 'yang.call/invoke-with callee positional named raise options)\n                      (list 'yang.call/invoke callee positional named raise))]\n     (list 'let [phase (list 'cell/new false)\n                 transfers (list 'cell/new 0) after (list 'cell/new false)]\n           (list (list 'fn [escape]\n                       (list 'if (list 'cell/get phase)\n                             escape\n                             (list 'do (list 'cell/set! phase true)\n                                   (list 'let [returned invocation]\n                                         (list 'do (list 'cell/set! after true)\n                                               (observation-map-form\n                                                 {:route :return :value returned\n                                                  :transfers (list 'cell/get transfers)\n                                                  :after (list 'cell/get after)}))))))\n                 (list '%capture))))))\n\n\n\n(defn run-typescript-identity-store\n  \"Run one identity-store probe kind against the TypeScript donor on\n   all three linked vector VMs; answers {backend observation}.\"\n  [kind]\n  (try\n    (let [donor @boundary-donor]\n      (kit/run-exception-program\n        donor\n        (kit/compose-exception donor [\"boundary_target\"] :typescript\n                               (contract/sources :typescript)\n                               (identity-store-observation-form kind))))\n    (catch Throwable e\n      (kit/error-results e))))\n\n\n(defn run-fixture\n  \"One source-created receiver per task. All three linked vector VMs run.\n   A fresh task prevents a deliberately broken bridge from poisoning the\n   next fixture's handler context.\"\n  [{:keys [frontend source] :as fixture}]\n  (try\n    (let [donor @boundary-donor]\n      (kit/run-exception-program\n        donor\n        (kit/compose-exception donor [\"boundary_target\"] frontend source\n                               (observation-form fixture))))\n    (catch Throwable e\n      (kit/error-results e))))\n\n\n(defn run-frontend\n  \"Run one source unit per frontend and observe each fixture's separate\n   public activations. Full context snapshot proof remains a frontend gate.\n   `saved` is intentionally task-owned: lifetime probes\n   must finish retain before entering later. `run-fixture` remains available\n   for an isolated diagnostic when a frontend's broken state poisons a batch.\"\n  [frontend]\n  (let [fixtures (filter #(= frontend (:frontend %)) contract/fixtures)]\n    (try\n      (let [donor @boundary-donor\n            observations (reduce (fn [acc fixture]\n                                   (list 'assoc acc (:id fixture) (observation-form fixture)))\n                                 {} fixtures)\n            results (kit/run-exception-program\n                      donor\n                      (kit/compose-exception donor [\"boundary_target\"] frontend\n                                             (contract/sources frontend) observations))]\n        (if (some #(instance? Throwable %) (vals results))\n          ;; An operational defect is not a source exception. Isolate fixtures\n          ;; so one host refusal neither erases nor invents the other outcomes.\n          (into {} (for [{:keys [id] :as fixture} fixtures]\n                     [id (run-fixture fixture)]))\n          (into {} (for [{:keys [id]} fixtures]\n                     [id (update-vals results #(get % id))]))))\n      (catch Throwable e\n        (let [err (kit/error-results e)]\n          (into {} (for [{:keys [id]} fixtures]\n                     [id err])))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
