llab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:40:operation in this reproduction needs that doubled value. This is not genuinely unsupported\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:41:count state: the runtime just produced it from an admitted count, and both ownership\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:55:Every operation constructing that count is an admitted integer-module operation and stays\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:56:inside its configured limit. No raw-host arithmetic or over-limit intermediate is needed.\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:69:No count edits, guest numeric operations, or condition changes occur between receptions.\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:73:| Initial count | Initially admitted | First identity / class | Admitted after first return | Second identity / class |\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:84:For the failing T-1 row, the count after the first return has 100000 magnitude bits,\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:85:and BOTH integer/add(count,1) and integer/sub(count,1) return exact integers.\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:93:{:before-double-integer true\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:94: :after-double :yin.vm.integer/bit-limit\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:101:The probe is sound as an immediate arithmetic safety margin: for B>=4096, passing doubling\\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:103:before the ACTUAL ari