Reaching it from a minted count (`:rc 1`) takes `2^B` acquisitions; only a\\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:95:deliberately constructed count of magnitude ≈2^(B-1) starts within one acquisition of it. **Local\\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:96:identity is therefore claimed while a count stays operable, not unconditionally** — that is the\\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:103:| T1 | `php-count-acquisition-test`: shapes generalised from `[label digits]` to `[label count-form]`; four `integer/parse` forms now written explicitly, bodies unchanged | the four r11 shapes assert exactly what they asserted at 2da48669 — sol's Ruling 3 accepted those assertions, so nothing was re-worded |\\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:105:| T3 | `count-source` docstring | names the fifth count and why it must stay local across both receptions. The PHP source itself is unchanged (`catch_return`, `is_local_exception`) |\\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:106:| T4 | `php-count-acquisition-test` header comment | records the r12 addition and the new key count |\\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:107:| T5 | `php-count-limit-test` comment | no longer claims a doubling/headroom probe; states that this test is the half of the limit policy that must NOT be deleted with the doubling, and cross-references `t-minus-one` for the other half. **Its assertions are unchanged**: `:rc` = `(+ (integer/shift-left 1 99999) (integer/shift-left 1 99999))` = 2^100000 stays FOREIGN with the four full-retention observations (returned wrapper, `is_foreign`, whole condition incl. `{:complete [:evidence]}`, payload identity through a later activation) |\\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r