er\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe bounds are PHP'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s signed 64-bit bounds, not every host'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s native arithmetic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbounds. The prelude'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s own value-encoding documentation and dao.host.integer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexplicitly specify a JS BigInt carrier beyond the safe Number range.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor example, integer/parse of \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"9007199254740992\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" produces a JS BigInt. It is an\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ninteger, is strictly inside both checked bounds, and php/int? classifies it as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n:int. Reception then reaches raw (+ rc 1). The VM registers the host + directly;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\non JS this mixes BigInt rc with Number 1.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFirsthand Node primitive diagnostic, both signs:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n9007199254740992  inside-signed-64-bit-bounds: true\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTypeError Cannot mix BigInt and other types, use explicit conversions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n-9007199254740992 inside-signed-64-bit-bounds: true\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTypeError Cannot mix BigInt and other types, use explicit conversions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis is a native-operation reproduction plus source tracing, not a claim that\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe complete Node boundary harness was run. The same decimal count completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe JVM direct local-reception 