n namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nexit 0\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n55:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_27\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cat collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md; sed -n '565,610p' src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '2923,2945p'; nl -ba test/yang/call/php_exception_test.clj | sed -n '625,670p'; sed -n '220,235p' collab/exception-track/1794446270000-architect-php-r1r2r3-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Created-GMT: 2026-11-07 04:30:00 GMT\\\\\\\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-07 11:30:00 +07 (+0700)\\\\\\\\nStatus: OWNER-APPROVED 2026-11-07 (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"enforce everywhere consistently. this should be a separate track.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"); v2 SUPERSEDES v1 (1794920000000) per the review round — architect gpt-6-astra, engineer mob gpt-6.1-sol + gemini-3.8-flash: all three ACCEPT WITH AMENDMENTS, folded below. Qwen aborted (headless tool denial); kimi quota-exhausted (429).\\\\\\\\nReview records: collab/exception-track/1794930000000-architect-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gemini-3.8-flash.stdout.log.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# RULING OF RECORD v2 — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## The decision\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nException handling is enforced uniformly across yang.clojure, yang.typescript (js),\\\\\\\\nyang.php, and yang.python. At every admitted guest-call boundary, an escaping source\\\\\\\\nexception compiles down to THE SAME continuation: the caller's supplied raise exit\\\\\\\\nreceiving the §8.10.7 condition\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value original-thrown-value}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nand every receiving runtime implements the §8.10.7 reception rules as written. This is a\\\\\\\\nSEPARATE TRACK: its own folder (collab/exception-track/), its own rounds, its own\\\\\\\\nacceptance gate; the four frontend seats cede the exception-fix surfaces to the track and\\\\\\\\nreceive per-frontend results back into their records.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Scope bounds (v2: sharpened per astra §5)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Every boundary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" means ADMITTED GUEST-CALL boundaries. VM/custody defects and host\\\\\\\\n  implementation failures remain operational failures (design :3904); no broad\\\\\\\\n  host catch-and-relabel is authorized.\\\\\\\\n- A RETURNED condition-shaped map is ordinary data; a THROWN condition-shaped map is the\\\\\\\\n  payload of a fresh condition; shape is never evidence of an existing condition to\\\\\\\\n  forward (the cell-ref rule, restated — R5).\\\\\\\\n- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Same continuation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" does NOT require identical internal lowering (R4's allowance).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## The requirements (v2: amended per the review round)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**R1 — the callee bridge (js AND php non-compliant today).** Every frontend's published\\\\\\\\nfunction entry, closure entry, and higher-order entry installs the exception bridge\\\\\\\\nBEFORE argument binding: it reads the supplied `:yang.call/raise` and delivers every\\\\\\\\nescaping source exception AND argument-binding failure to it as the thrown condition,\\\\\\\\nexactly once, with execution after the call unreachable. js entries apply `:code` without\\\\\\\\nreading the raise exit (prelude.cljc:1581); php's function entry (:2264) and Closure entry\\\\\\\\n(:4217) lack it, and php's raise with an empty handler stack RETURNS normally\\\\\\\\n(prelude.cljc:194-197). The bridge must also satisfy §8.10.8: complete cleanup and\\\\\\\\nhandler/depth/frame restoration BEFORE the transfer; a later generator resume never\\\\\\\\nreuses a raise exit belonging to a completed call.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**R2 — foreign reception and retained-condition lifetime (python, php non-compliant\\\\\\\\ntoday).** On receiving a thrown condition: (1) a payload valid in the receiving runtime\\\\\\\\nkeeps its ordinary catching and identity behavior — delivered UNCHANGED (python raising\\\\\\\\nan already-local exception raw is compliant; python raising an OTHERWISE-FOREIGN payload\\\\\\\\nraw at :1034 is not); (2) js may deliver the otherwise-foreign payload raw; (3) python\\\\\\\\nand php represent an otherwise-foreign payload with their own generated\\\\\\\\n`ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original payload — catch-all\\\\\\\\ncatches it, typed catches match the LOCAL hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names,\\\\\\\\nand formatting it never implicitly invokes foreign methods. Retention rides the generated\\\\\\\\nexception's IDENTITY for its ENTIRE LIFETIME, outside source-writable attributes, with no\\\\\\\\nambient registry (design :3878, :3885). Raising the whole envelope (php :2384) or an\\\\\\\\notherwise-foreign raw payload (python :1034) is non-compliant.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**R3 — protocol failures retain and forward the condition (ALL FOUR frontends; v2\\\\\\\\nwidened per astra §1 / sol §1).** `:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`,\\\\\\\\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding` (fully qualified) map to a documented local exception\\\\\\\\nform retaining the complete original condition — qualified reason AND plain evidence — so\\\\\\\\nan unchanged rethrow FORWARDS the original condition without a new wrapper. js discards\\\\\\\\nthe condition into fresh text (:1627); python builds a generic TypeError (:1046); clojure\\\\\\\\nretains it as catch data (:1306) but public escape reclassifies through unconditional\\\\\\\\n`yang.call/thrown` (:1088); php constructs a fresh Error for not-callable and raises the\\\\\\\\nenvelope otherwise (:2384), and its source rethrow rejects that envelope (:4085). All\\\\\\\\nfour are in scope, reception AND outbound rethrow.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**R4 — clojure unifies or proves equivalence.** The intra-unit outcome-token channel\\\\\\\\n(clojure.cljc:1115, :1125-1133) may remain an optimization only with equivalence proof\\\\\\\\nacross caught/uncaught throws, protocol rethrow, binding failures, and higher-order\\\\\\\\nre-entry (§8.10.9's bar) — a single passing example is insufficient. Public\\\\\\\\nprotocol-rethrow repair (R3) does not wait for this decision. Clojure's restricted catch\\\\\\\\nsurface (single catch, no `finally`) is a source-semantics decision this ruling does not\\\\\\\\nchange.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**R5 — no new shape-routing.** Per the scope bounds above; plus: forged or\\\\\\\\nsource-writable attributes on a wrapper-looking value never authenticate a retained\\\\\\\\ncondition.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## The baseline (audit of record)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe gpt-6.1-sol audit (collab/yang-python/1794900000000, verdict DIVERGENT, HEAD\\\\\\\\ne9a0b430) is the baseline. Citation corrections of record from the review round: js\\\\\\\\nfollows its GUEST continuation handler stack (js.rt/ctx, prelude.cljc:1704), not the host\\\\\\\\nengine's; php's empty-stack return is :194-197 (envelope reception :2384); clojure's\\\\\\\\nactual private branches are :1115 and :1125-1133 (:1110 is the packet-length guard).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Acceptance gate (v2: widened per astra §4 / sol §4)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe track is DONE when ALL of the following hold, with real source on both sides of every\\\\\\\\nleg:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **The directed pair matrix — 12 cross-language directions** derived from the four\\\\\\\\n   admitted frontends (clojure↔python and clojure↔php explicitly included), plus local\\\\\\\\n   regressions.\\\\\\\\n2. **Callable-kind coverage**: named exports AND closure/higher-order entries (php\\\\\\\\n   Closures concretely), supported methods/callable objects per frontend capability.\\\\\\\\n3. **The §8.10.11 exception scenarios**: binding failures; arbitrary foreign thrown\\\\\\\\n   data; catch-all and typed catches (where the source has them — js has no typed-catch\\\\\\\\n   syntax, clojure's admitted surface rejects `finally`; exercise cleanup in a frontend\\\\\\\\n   that supports it and PRESERVE clojure's rejection tests); unchanged rethrow; finally\\\\\\\\n   replacement; protocol-error rethrow; condition-shaped thrown maps staying data;\\\\\\\\n   A→B→A propagation asserting original identity and cleanup order; the stored\\\\\\\\n   ForeignException rethrown from another activation.\\\\\\\\n4. **Context lifetime**: repeated success→raise→success, cross-runtime recursion,\\\\\\\\n   suspension/resume — handler/depth/frame state restored, exactly-once\\\\\\\\n   binding/cleanup.\\\\\\\\n5. **Host-by-VM results**: JVM, Node, and Dart across the admitted VM paths, with\\\\\\\\n   explicit refusals; portable parser-produced fixtures where the JVM-only kit cannot\\\\\\\\n   reach; bundled-walker paths where admitted, never requiring unsupported linked\\\\\\\\n   execution; bundled/linked parity and task isolation preserving existing custody\\\\\\\\n   refusals.\\\\\\\\n6. **Identity assertions BEFORE rendering**: original reasons, complete evidence, payload\\\\\\\\n   identity, wrapper non-stacking, cleanup order — equal rendered text is not identity\\\\\\\\n   evidence.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Sequencing (v2: corrected per astra §3 / sol §3 — the v1 order is REJECTED)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n0. Contract + focused FAILING fixtures first (retained-condition provenance; boundary\\\\\\\\n   fixtures construct malformed invocations source cannot naturally build).\\\\\\\\n1. **JS R1 + R3** together (R3 alone cannot cross the boundary while entries ignore the\\\\\\\\n   exit).\\\\\\\\n2. **PHP R1 + R2 + R3 as ONE coherent round** — function entry, Closure entry, and all\\\\\\\\n   three call helpers (php/call, call-with-binding-profile, call-named). Landing the\\\\\\\\n   bridge before reception repair would route local Throwables into the envelope-raising\\\\\\\\n   receiver and break existing local typed catches.\\\\\\\\n3. **Python R2 + R3 with the egress change** (prelude.cljc:912's always-fresh condition\\\\\\\\n   must become condition-preserving for retained wrappers).\\\\\\\\n4. **Clojure R3, then R4** (the optimization decision last).\\\\\\\\nJS and Python work proceed independently once the contract lands; no Clojure-containing\\\\\\\\npair declares conformance before its R3 gap closes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n— filed by the yang.python orchestrator seat; owner decision 2026-11-07\\\\\\\\n      (refuse! 'decimal->float :syntax {}))\\\\\\\\n    (float-kernel/decimal->float (digit-values! 'decimal->float digits 10) e)))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- int-max-digits\\\\\\\\n  [limits]\\\\\\\\n  (::max-digits limits))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n;; Recognition\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- int-integer?\\\\\\\\n  [_limits x]\\\\\\\\n  (host/exact-integer? x))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- int-normalize\\\\\\\\n  [limits a]\\\\\\\\n  (out limits (big! 'normalize 0 a)))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n;; The module\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(def ^:private exports\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`[name arities kernel]` of every export. Each kernel takes the\\\\\\\\n   composition's limits first.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  [['integer? [1] int-integer?]\\\\\\\\n   ['normalize [1] int-normalize]\\\\\\\\n   ['add [2] int-add]\\\\\\\\n   ['sub [2] int-sub]\\\\\\\\n   ['neg [1] int-neg]\\\\\\\\n   ['mul [2] int-mul]\\\\\\\\n   ['compare [2] int-compare]\\\\\\\\n   ['quot-rem [2] int-quot-rem]\\\\\\\\n   ['floor-div-mod [2] int-floor-div-mod]\\\\\\\\n   ['pow [2] int-pow]\\\\\\\\n   ['bit-and [2] int-bit-and]\\\\\\\\n   ['bit-or [2] int-bit-or]\\\\\\\\n   ['bit-xor [2] int-bit-xor]\\\\\\\\n   ['bit-not [1] int-bit-not]\\\\\\\\n   ['shift-left [2] int-shift-left]\\\\\\\\n   ['shift-right [2] int-shift-right]\\\\\\\\n  2923\\\\\\\\t           (if (cell/authentic? (get v :php/obj))\\\\\\\\n  2924\\\\\\\\t             (let [st (cell/get (get v :php/obj))]\\\\\\\\n  2925\\\\\\\\t               (if (data/string? (get st :class))\\\\\\\\n  2926\\\\\\\\t                 (let [rc (get st :rc)]\\\\\\\\n  2927\\\\\\\\t                   ;; integer/integer? FIRST: it is the total domain\\\\\\\\n  2928\\\\\\\\t                   ;; predicate of the integer/compare below and of the\\\\\\\\n  2929\\\\\\\\t                   ;; integer/add and integer/sub the count arithmetic\\\\\\\\n  2930\\\\\\\\t                   ;; uses, and all three refuse any carrier it rejects.\\\\\\\\n  2931\\\\\\\\t                   ;; A php representation classifier cannot stand in for\\\\\\\\n  2932\\\\\\\\t                   ;; it: a computed ratio passes data/number? AND php/int?\\\\\\\\n  2933\\\\\\\\t                   ;; (php/kind's float64 content test), and integer/compare\\\\\\\\n  2934\\\\\\\\t                   ;; then refuses it — the reception-introduced failure of\\\\\\\\n  2935\\\\\\\\t                   ;; the re-check4 counterexample.\\\\\\\\n  2936\\\\\\\\t                   (if (integer/integer? rc)\\\\\\\\n  2937\\\\\\\\t                     (if (= (integer/compare rc php.rt/int-max) -1)\\\\\\\\n  2938\\\\\\\\t                       (= (integer/compare rc php.rt/int-min) 1)\\\\\\\\n  2939\\\\\\\\t                       false)\\\\\\\\n  2940\\\\\\\\t                     false))\\\\\\\\n  2941\\\\\\\\t                 false))\\\\\\\\n  2942\\\\\\\\t             false))))]\\\\\\\\n  2943\\\\\\\\t    [php.rt/receive-condition\\\\\\\\n  2944\\\\\\\\t     ;; §8.10.7 reception, shared by every php call helper: classify the\\\\\\\\n  2945\\\\\\\\t     ;; delivered condition and continue it as a local Throwable. A\\\\\\\\n   625\\\\\\\\t  ;; above (rule 3), retained with their complete condition, evidence and\\\\\\\\n   626\\\\\\\\t  ;; payload identity.\\\\\\\\n   627\\\\\\\\t  (let [shapes [[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"near-max\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"9223372036854775806\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\n   628\\\\\\\\t                [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"js-number-boundary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"9007199254740992\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]]\\\\\\\\n   629\\\\\\\\t        leg (fn [[label digits]]\\\\\\\\n   630\\\\\\\\t              (let [n (fn [k] (symbol (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"probe.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (name label) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (name k))))\\\\\\\\n   631\\\\\\\\t                    p (n :payload) c (n :condition) i (n :injected) r (n :result)]\\\\\\\\n   632\\\\\\\\t                {:bindings [p (kit/observation-map-form\\\\\\\\n   633\\\\\\\\t                                {:php/obj (list 'cell/new\\\\\\\\n   634\\\\\\\\t                                                (list 'assoc {:class \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Exception\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\n   635\\\\\\\\t                                                      :rc (list 'integer/parse digits)))})\\\\\\\\n   636\\\\\\\\t                            c (kit/observation-map-form\\\\\\\\n   637\\\\\\\\t                                {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\\\\\\\\n   638\\\\\\\\t                                 :yang.call/value p})\\\\\\\\n   639\\\\\\\\t                            i (injected c)\\\\\\\\n   640\\\\\\\\t                            r (boundary-call (kit/export-form :php \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"catch_return\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") [i])]\\\\\\\\n   641\\\\\\\\t                 :entries {(keyword (str label \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-returned\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\n   642\\\\\\\\t                           (list '= :return (list 'get r :route))\\\\\\\\n   643\\\\\\\\t                           (keyword (str label \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-identical\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\n   644\\\\\\\\t                           (list '= p (list 'get r :value))}}))\\\\\\\\n   645\\\\\\\\t        legs (map leg shapes)\\\\\\\\n   646\\\\\\\\t        observation (kit/guard-exceptions-form\\\\\\\\n   647\\\\\\\\t                      [:php]\\\\\\\\n   648\\\\\\\\t                      (list 'let (into [] (mapcat :bindings) legs)\\\\\\\\n   649\\\\\\\\t                            (kit/observation-map-form (into {} (mapcat :entries) legs))))\\\\\\\\n   650\\\\\\\\t        expected (into {} (mapcat (fn [[label _]]\\\\\\\\n   651\\\\\\\\t                                    (map (fn [k] [(keyword (str label \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" k)) true])\\\\\\\\n   652\\\\\\\\t                                         [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"returned\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"identical\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]))\\\\\\\\n   653\\\\\\\\t                                  shapes))\\\\\\\\n   654\\\\\\\\t        donor (kit/publish-donor! :python contract/boundary-source)\\\\\\\\n   655\\\\\\\\t        results (kit/run-exception-program\\\\\\\\n   656\\\\\\\\t                  donor (kit/compose-exception donor [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"boundary_target\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"] :php\\\\\\\\n   657\\\\\\\\t                                               count-source observation))]\\\\\\\\n   658\\\\\\\\t    (is (= #{:semantic :stack :register} (set (keys results))))\\\\\\\\n   659\\\\\\\\t    (doseq [[backend actual] results]\\\\\\\\n   660\\\\\\\\t      (println \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PHP-COUNT-ACQUISITION\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" backend actual)\\\\\\\\n   661\\\\\\\\t      (is (= expected actual)\\\\\\\\n   662\\\\\\\\t          (str backend \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": every boundary count survives ordinary catch/return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   663\\\\\\\\t               \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"acquisition with identity preserved\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))))\\\\\\\\n   664\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   665\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   666\\\\\\\\t(deftest ^:slow php-nil-condition-reception-test\\\\\\\\n   667\\\\\\\\t  ;; The steward addendum's F1 nil-guard choice, taken DELIBERATELY as\\\\\\\\n   668\\\\\\\\t  ;; option (a): a non-map or nil condition delivered to reception is NOT\\\\\\\\n   669\\\\\\\\t  ;; provenance-minted (nil provenance is refused by the reserved door —\\\\\\\\n   670\\\\\\\\t  ;; an operational failure that would escape the boundary behavior); it\\\\\\\\neight exception-track briefs/spec/findings records. Runtime regions are function entry,\\\\\\\\nClosure entry, reception through the three helpers, retention helpers, host-door declaration,\\\\\\\\nand the seeded exception hierarchy. This is consistent with the supplied PHP round and\\\\\\\\nadoption briefs. No shared kit, design doctrine, scanner golden, ledger, or other frontend\\\\\\\\nimplementation was edited. `git diff --check 0e666a3f..4939a3ae` passed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe referenced region registry\\\\\\\\n`collab/exception-track/1794343000000-exception-track-surface-registry.md` is absent from\\\\\\\\nthis worktree and from the reviewed base. Its literal region list cannot be certified here;\\\\\\\\nscope was checked against the available binding briefs and actual diff instead.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nGate tables are plausible as scoped engineer reports, not independently reproduced gate\\\\\\\\nresults. The hard-rule parity pin (:298) uses the kit boundary and parsed PHP bare rethrow,\\\\\\\\nasserts the fully qualified reason and condition identity, and checks all three backends.\\\\\\\\nThe clone/mutation pins inspect guest identity before rendering. Test data and assertions\\\\\\\\nwere not weakened by r2/r3. The reported Node/Dart/remote and slow-corpus gaps are explicit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n59:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_30\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\\\\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\\\\\\\\np=Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/private/tmp/phpexc-review/collab/exception-track/1794527358000-architect-step7-recheck5.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\nassert not p.exists(), \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Refusing to overwrite an existing findings artifact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nnow=datetime.now(timezone.utc)\\\\\\\\nheader=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Created-GMT: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+now.strftime(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCreated-Local: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+now.astimezone(timezone(timedelta(hours=7))).strftime(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S +0700 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\np.write_text(header+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Coding-Agent: codex (gpt-6.1-sol)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSession-ID: unavailable in this environment\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRole: Architect, read-only step-7 re-check round 5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nReviewed-Base: 265c4a4590259f2ea592cb81cd6991aa7b8afde8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nReviewed-Tip: 59329a054a66041cb2c5816aae0e97dc65e2b542\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVerdict: RESIDUALS — NOT MERGE-READY\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n# Step-7 re-check round 5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe exact-integer repair closes both concrete count-domain defects from re-check 4:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nordinary acquisition no longer uses native overflowing/mixed-carrier arithmetic, and a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncomputed Ratio is rejected before integer/compare. However, I rule AGAINST the restored\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nendpoint disposition. One P2 residual remains: a value admitted and returned as the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noriginal local Exception becomes ForeignException on its next ordinary reception because\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe first reception moved its count onto the excluded maximum. This was reproduced\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthrough parsed/lowered PHP source at the reviewed tip.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source and tests were reviewed read-only. Only this requested findings artifact was\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwritten; no source, tests, fixtures, configuration, caches, or git history were modified.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## P2 residual — ordinary ownership changes turn a local exception into a foreign one\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nLocation: src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2937-2939.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nConsumer: php.rt/receive-condition at :2975-2977.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCoverage gap: test/yang/call/php_exception_test.clj:627-644 exercises only one reception.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe test'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s own near-max payload is sufficient:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```clojure'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(assoc {} :php/obj\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       (cell/new (assoc {:class \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Exception\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       :rc (integer/parse \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"9223372036854775806\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSupply its thrown condition through a callable'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s actual :yang.call/raise exit, and call\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthis ordinary PHP receiver TWICE with the same callable/condition:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction receive(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$f) {'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    try { return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$f(); }'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    catch (Throwable \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$e) { return $e; }'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nKeep the first returned value live while making the second call. No count edits, numeric\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noperations, or malformed-condition tricks occur between the two calls. Firsthand results\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfrom current-tip source, production host registry and JVM AST walker:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Initial count | First result identical | Count after first return | Second result identical | Second class |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| 1 | true | 2 | true | Exception |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| 9223372036854775806 | true | 9223372036854775807 | **false** | **ForeignException** |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| 9007199254740992 | true | 9007199254740993 | true | Exception |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe failing case completed normally at the VM level; this is a semantic identity failure,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot another host overflow. Its count after the second call remains 9223372036854775807.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nA separate parserless two-reception probe gave the same classification failure.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe first call proves exactly why the engineer'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s claim that the endpoint is \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"not a count\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nphp'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s machinery could have produced\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" is false: php'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s own repaired ownership operations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\njust produced it. The value is still throwable by php/throw-value, which checks the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThrowable hierarchy and uses the repaired exact addref. Only boundary reception changes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nits class/identity. An ordinary catch retaining one more reference cannot make an otherwise\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nunchanged local exception foreign.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Endpoint ruling\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSection 8.10.7 rule 1 and the owner ruling v2 R2 require already-local exceptions to retain\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nordinary catching and identity. Rule 3 applies to an OTHERWISE-foreign payload; it does\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot authorize reclassifying this runtime-produced state just because its private reference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncount reached the source-language integer endpoint.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe accepted Python implementation at prelude.cljc:1067-1079 recognizes its own exception\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrepresentation/hierarchy and raises that value unchanged. It has no PHP reference-count\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nanalogue that would justify a signed-64-bit cutoff on PHP'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s now-exact ownership arithmetic.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPHP still needs representation and operability checks; that does not make every previous\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncount cutoff a semantic invariant after its original arithmetic reason has been removed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI therefore rule the other way on the handover question: the signed-64-bit endpoints,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nby themselves, are not a reason to wrap an otherwise admitted Throwable under the repaired\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\narithmetic. The positive maximum counterexample alone is enough to reject the restored\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npolicy. The minimum-only exclusion likewise lacks the old decrement-overflow justification;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nany separately proposed count invariant must be justified consistently, not inferred from\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe old host carrier limits.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRequired completion:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Preserve exact integer/add and integer/sub and the exact-integer admission predicate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Make reception preserve local type/identity across ordinary acquisitions and later\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  receptions, including the runtime-produced endpoint and beyond-native results.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Extend the near-max source pin to two calls while the first result remains live, with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  original identity and original Exception class on BOTH results.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Keep endpoint coverage, but revise its asserted disposition under this ruling instead\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  of deleting the cases. Keep malformed, competing-marker, ratio, missing/non-number and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  legitimate-local controls with complete-condition/evidence/payload checks for foreign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  cases.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis revises the old endpoint disposition explicitly in response to the requested ruling;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nit is not permission to silently invert or remove unrelated pins.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Do not apply the documented bare revert without a limit-aware replacement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe engineer is correct about the separate integer-module limit hazard: integer/integer?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrecognizes carriers without checking ::integer/max-bits; integer/add and integer/sub can\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreturn ::bit-limit. Installing that keyword as :rc would make the next integer operation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrefuse. Merely deleting both bounds and accepting EVERY exact integer is not a complete fix.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThat hazard does not justify the particular strict 64-bit boundary: MAX, MAX+1 and MIN are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwell inside the profile'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s minimum 4096-bit arithmetic limit. Count validation/limit handling\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmust distinguish genuinely unsupported state from the local results ordinary ownership\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnow produces. No broad host catch is authorized.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTwo details in the findings'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' supporting argument should also be corrected:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(1) raw clojure.core/* on two Long operands does not auto-promote past overflow; a BigInt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nseed is needed for the proposed repeated-squaring construction; (2) an initial 63-bit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbound does not prove ALL subsequent ownership results stay 64-bit. Neither correction\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnegates the real ::bit-limit hazard, and neither is the blocking reproduction above.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Ruling 1 — both re-check-4 count-domain counterexamples are repaired\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nphp/addref (:1856-1857) and php/delref (:1869) now use the integer module. Its checked big\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npath promotes operands to the host big carrier, computes exactly, and demotes to the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncanonical carrier; its fast path falls back when the safe native result range is exceeded.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe ordinary lower-return acquisition still calls php/addref (lower.cljc:2945), so the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrepair applies after reception as required, including copying/rethrow operations using it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source receiver above now completes its FIRST near-max call with original identity;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe previous native-long overflow is closed. The 2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^53 decimal also completes with original'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nidentity through both calls on the JVM.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor JS, dao.host.integer/exact-integer? admits BigInt, promote keeps both arithmetic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noperands in BigInt form, and demote produces the canonical Number/BigInt result. Thus the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncount is no longer sent to raw BigInt-plus-Number arithmetic. integer/sub demotes zero to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe native zero, preserving the existing (= n 0) destruction test. This is verified by\\\\\\\\\\\\