d remaining gate disposition\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFirsthand this round:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Full requested source/test diff, re-check 4, r10 findings, governing architecture,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  §8.10.7, owner ruling v2, accepted Python reception and relevant integer/ownership/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  lowering implementations inspected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Bounded current-source JVM diagnostics completed with exit 0: direct count controls\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  and the parsed/lowered receiver called twice with three count controls.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Static surface/adoption/reachability pins: 3 tests, 14 passes, 0 failures, 0 errors.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- git diff --check 265c4a45..59329a05 passed; tracked working-tree status remained clean.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source probe borrowed only existing generated parser class directories from the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nphpexc checkout, plus cached dependency jars; current worktree source/test roots led\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe classpath. PHP manifest.edn and PhpParser.g4 match that checkout byte-for-byte.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNo builds, generated files, dependency resolution or cache writes were performed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTwo preliminary source-probe attempts had diagnostic-script setup/read errors; the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreported source table is from the corrected, successful bounded invocation, not those\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nattempts. The parserless identity failure was independently observed as well.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe orchestrator'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s tip gate evidence in the dispatch is accepted as supplied evidence:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfocused count/nil/shape/