voking'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe destructor. The raw subtraction at :4386 therefore does not consume the large count\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nadmitted from a boundary. Under ordinary PHP ownership, only acquisitions/releases made\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nduring this destructor contribute to its unpin value.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI accept that scoped argument for the requested residual: the near-max and JS-BigInt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreceived-carrier counterexamples cannot flow into this subtraction. No conversion is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrequired for this review. This is not a proof against arbitrary guest cell/set\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'! corruption'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nduring a destructor, nor an unrestricted totality claim for an unbounded number of\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nacquisitions. Neither is the counterexample established here.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Ruling 4 — pins, publication surface and scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe requested range is one commit and exactly three changed files: the PHP prelude,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe PHP exception test, and the r10 findings. No other frontend, VM implementation,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlowerer, shared kit, fixture, ledger, or design file changes in this range.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNo previous assertion or payload case is removed. The two original endpoint payload\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nforms remain, with their foreign-retention observations; the computed-ratio case and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe ordinary catch/return acquisition test are additive. The committed shape matrix is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnow TWELVE cases with FOUR observations each (48 expected keys per backend), rather than\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe supplied gate summary'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s 45-key description. I did not inspect that remote batch'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nraw output and do not equate these cardinalities; the direct ratio result above is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfirsthand evidence of the repaired ratio path.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAdding integer/integer? to host-names declares an already-existing integer module export,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot a new PHP publication door. Removing data/number? removes an unused declaration.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe PHP exports, aliases, reserved provenance doors, receiver/mint privacy and mint call\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ngraph are unchanged. There is no broad host catch or arbitrary-condition mint helper.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\naddref/delref are outside the original receiver'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s textual region, but changing ownership\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noperations is expressly required by re-check 4'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s whole-consumption-path residual and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthis dispatch. No unrelated ownership algorithm changed. The literal surface-registry\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfile 1794343000000 remains absent here, as disclosed in the original review; scope is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nchecked against the available binding briefs and the actual diff, not a nonexistent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nregistry artifact.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Evidence and remaining gate disposition\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFirsthand this round:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Full requested source/test diff, re-check 4, r10 findings, governing architecture,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  §8.10.7, owner ruling v2, accepted Python reception and relevant integer/ownership/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  lowering implementations inspected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Bounded current-source JVM diagnostics completed with exit 0: direct count controls\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  and the parsed/lowered receiver called twice with three count controls.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Static surface/adoption/reachability pins: 3 tests, 14 passes, 0 failures, 0 errors.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- git diff --check 265c4a45..59329a05 passed; tracked working-tree status remained clean.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source probe borrowed only existing generated parser class directories from the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nphpexc checkout, plus cached dependency jars; current worktree source/test roots led\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe classpath. PHP manifest.edn and PhpParser.g4 match that checkout byte-for-byte.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNo builds, generated files, dependency resolution or cache writes were performed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTwo preliminary source-probe attempts had diagnostic-script setup/read errors; the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreported source table is from the corrected, successful bounded invocation, not those\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nattempts. The parserless identity failure was independently observed as well.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe orchestrator'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s tip gate evidence in the dispatch is accepted as supplied evidence:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfocused count/nil/shape/directed/adoption/reachability batches, listed namespaces, kondo\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nand cljstyle. Those successes cover the existing assertions; a one-reception count pin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndoes not exercise the newly demonstrated second reception. I did not rerun the linked\\\\\\\\\\