y). The\\\\n   producer carries float kind; the codec never infers it.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  (cbor/float64 (float-value x)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- callable?\\\\n  \\\\\\\"True when `x` can be applied: a host function, a closure or a\\\\n   continuation. A map is never callable, whatever keys it carries.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  (or (fn? x) (values/closure? x) (values/continuation? x)))\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  (or (integer/exact-integer? x)\\\\n      #?(:cljs (and (number? x) (js/Number.isInteger x)\\\\n                    (not (js/Number.isSafeInteger x)))\\\\n         :default false)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn float64?\\\\n  \\\\\\\"True for floating-point content: Double or Float on the JVM, the\\\\n   Float64 carrier or a non-integral, non-finite or negative-zero number\\\\n   on JavaScript, a double on Dart.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  #?(:cljd (dart/is? x double)\\\\n     :clj (or (instance? Double x) (instance? Float x))\\\\n     :cljs (or (instance? number/Float64 x)\\\\n               (and (number? x) (not (host-integer? x))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn decimal?\\\\n  \\\\\\\"True for decimal content: BigDecimal on the JVM, the Decimal carrier on\\\\n   JavaScript and Dart.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  (number/decimal? x))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn ratio?\\\\n  \\\\\\\"True for rational content: clojure.lang.Ratio or the Rational carrier.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  (number/ratio? x))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn numeric?\\\\n  \\\\\\\"True for every value the portable numeric operations accept.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  (or (host-integer? x) (float64? x) (decimal? x) (ratio? x)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn float64\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Floating-point content with the value of host number x: a Double on\\\\n   the JVM, the Float64 carrier on JavaScript (so integral floats such as\\\\n   1.0 keep their kind).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [x]\\\\n  (number/float64-of x))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn float64-from-bits\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Floating-point content with the IEEE-754 bits given as 16 lowercase\\\\n   hex digits.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [hex]\\\\n  (number/float64-of (host float/bits->float64 hex)))\\\\n\\\\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\\\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\\\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\\\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def integer-limits\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The ordinary JavaScript composition's `integer` limits.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn registry\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The full host registry a linked JavaScript composition registers: the\\\\n   `require` handler, then `cell`, `data`, `integer` under `limits`, and\\\\n   `stream` — the hook module `jssp` polls a signal stream, so the\\\\n   safepointed composition needs it even though `js` does not.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ([] (registry integer-limits))\\\\n  ([limits]\\\\n   (-> (module/default-registry)\\\\n       module/register-cell-module\\\\n       (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\\\\n       (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\\\\n       module/register-stream-module)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def published\\\\n  \\\\\\\"`js` published once into its own content store:\\\\n   `{:store s :result r :address a :call-address ca}`. `yang.call` is\\\\n   published first so `js` pins its shared calling runtime.\\\\\\\"\\\\n(def ^:private capability-secret \\\\\\\"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn make-stream\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The composition's stream constructor: a deterministic ring buffer, answering\\\\n   the create outcome the engine consumes. The lifecycle streams below come\\\\n   from this same constructor, so request consumption and response/diagnostic\\\\n   emission travel composition-supplied streams rather than vectors.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ([] (make-stream nil))\\\\n  ([capacity]\\\\n   (ringbuffer/create!\\\\n     {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,\\\\n      ringbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)})))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- check-ok!\\\\n  [result what]\\\\n  (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\\\n    (throw (ex-info (str \\\\\\\"PHP lifecycle stream failed: \\\\\\\" what) {:result result})))\\\\n  result)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- lifecycle-stream\\\\n  \\\\\\\"One open lifecycle stream handle from the composition's own constructor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [what]\\\\n  (:dao.stream/handle (check-ok! (make-stream) what)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn create-vm\\\\n  \\\\\\\"An AST walker composed with the harness's deterministic ring-buffer stream.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ([] (create-vm {}))\\\\n  ([opts]\\\\n   (ast-walker/create-vm\\\\n     (merge {:make-stream (fn [capacity] (make-stream capacity)),\\\\n             :capability-secret capability-secret}\\\\n            opts))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- new-memory-log\\\\n  []\\\\n  (let [result (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})]\\\\n    (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\\\n      (:dao.stream/handle result)\\\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\\\\\"PHP harness memory-log creation failed\\\\\\\" {:result result})))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- drain\\\\n  [handle]\\\\n  (let [start (get-in (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)\\\\n                      [:dao.stream/cursor])]\\\\n    (loop [cursor start, acc []]\\\\n      (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\\\\n        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\\\n          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result)\\\\n                 (conj acc (:dao.stream/value result)))\\\\n          acc)))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def integer-limits\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The `integer` limits the PHP compositions here install.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def data-limits {::data/max-items 1048576})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn host-registry\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The registry with the cell, data, integer and stream modules installed,\\\\n   admitted by the PHP profile. The stream module is what lets execution\\\\n   emit response and diagnostic records on composition-supplied 